          "english": "Despite his concerns about the risks __(31)__ to humans by technological progress, Bostrom is no luddite(科技进步反对者). In fact, he is a longtime __(32)__ of trans-humanism—the effort to improve the human condition, and even human nature itself, through technological means. In the long run he sees technology as a bridge, a bridge we humans must cross with great care, in order to reach new and better modes of being. In his work, Bostrom uses the tools of philosophy and mathematics, in __(33)__ , probability theory, to try and determine how we as a __(34)__ might achieve this safe passage. What follows is my conversation with Bostrom about some of the most interesting and worrying existential risks that humanity might __(35)__ in the decades and centuries to come, and about what we can do to make sure we outlast them.",
          "chinese": "尽管担心技术进步给人类带来的风险，博斯特罗姆并不是科技进步反对者。事实上，他长期倡导超人类主义，即通过技术手段改善人类的处境，甚至改善人类自身的本性。从长远来看，他把技术视为一座桥梁，一座我们人类必须格外谨慎地跨越的桥梁，以便抵达全新且更好的存在方式。在他的研究中，博斯特罗姆运用哲学和数学工具，尤其是概率论，试图确定作为一个物种的我们该如何实现这种安全过渡。以下是我与博斯特罗姆的谈话，内容涉及未来数十年乃至数百年间人类可能遭遇的一些最有趣、也最令人担忧的存亡风险，以及我们能够采取哪些措施来确保自己比这些风险存在得更久。",
